The divergence between equity volatility (VIX 27) and credit spreads (IG OAS 0.96, historically tight) is the key short-term read. The framework's warning signal — credit spreads widening while equities bounce — is not yet present. Credit markets are not confirming an equity distress signal. The 1-month NDX drawdown of 7.68% is a positioning and sentiment event, consistent with the framework's observation that no cash flow changed by a third in one morning.

New political risk has emerged: the US midterm elections produced a Democrat-controlled Congress, with data-center permitting and AI spending scrutiny becoming live policy issues. (1)

