Critical sensitivity: The framework correctly identifies useful life as the most sensitive assumption. At a 3-year life instead of 5 years, the 2026E required revenue rises to approximately $597B — well above current cloud revenue. GPU refresh cycles of 2–3 years are a live industry debate. (8)

Cumulative AI capex of $6–8 trillion from 2024–2030 will require monetization, while consumer and B2B demand could generate about $2.5 trillion in annual revenue. (9)

Only about 25% of companies using AI had an enterprise-wide strategy, and AI projects reportedly fail for one in four companies. (10)

Sector test conclusion: The 2025 build is defensible. The 2026 doubling requires cloud revenue to grow ~40–50% year-over-year to stay in balance. That is achievable if AI monetization accelerates, but it is not guaranteed. The gap is the mid-term risk, not an immediate crisis.

