EBITDA does not cover interest expense on an operating basis. FCF is deeply negative at -$20.4B, funded entirely by external capital. The bond stack carries coupons of 9–9.75% on the high-yield tranches, reflecting market pricing of significant credit risk. No maturities fall within 24 months, which removes the immediate refinancing trigger — but the business model requires continuous external funding to operate.

CoreWeave faces a sentiment problem that strong earnings alone cannot fix; investors are focused on neocloud funding sustainability and data-center permitting risk from the midterm elections. (11)

Framework scorecard: Scores 5 of 7 "likely final loser" criteria: negative FCF dependent on outside funding; operating profit does not cover interest; revenue concentrated in debt-funded customers; undifferentiated rented compute product; growth dependent on external financing. Treat as an option on refinancing, sized accordingly.

