Lumentum deal value $101.1B (all-stock, pending)

The Lumentum deal, announced 2 November 2026, is valued at approximately $101B — roughly 10.7x Marvell's own LTM revenue. It is structured entirely in stock. A competing Nvidia cash bid for Lumentum at $2B was announced in March 2026 and remains pending. The share dilution factor rose to 1.0265 in 2026 from 1.009 in 2025, already reflecting some dilution pressure before the Lumentum deal closes.

Framework scorecard: Marvell's standalone business passes the survival filter — positive FCF, low net debt, 59% gross margin, diversified AI chip exposure. The deal overhang is the framework's stated risk: value per share after the Lumentum share issuance depends entirely on what Lumentum contributes to combined earnings versus the dilution it imposes. Until the deal closes or is withdrawn, per-share value is uncertain. Treat as a good business with a binary deal outcome layered on top.

