*Reality Labs is not a meaningful AI revenue proxy; Meta has no separately disclosed AI revenue line.

All four generate substantial positive FCF. Alphabet and Meta carry net cash or near-zero net debt. Microsoft's net debt of $33.8B is modest relative to $85.9B of annual FCF. Amazon's FCF compression to $11.2B (from $35.5B in 2024) directly reflects the capex surge — AWS revenue of $128.7B is growing, but capex consumed the free cash flow.

ROIC for Alphabet (25%), Microsoft (26.3%), and Meta (21.9%) remains well above any reasonable cost of capital estimate. Amazon's 12.3% ROIC is lower and declining, consistent with a heavy investment phase.

Framework scorecard: All four pass the survival filter with significant margin. The long-term question — whether ROIC holds above cost of capital as capex doubles in 2026 — is unanswerable today. The capex-to-revenue ratio will be the metric to track at Q4 2026 earnings.

